1.14.1 Release notes (2026-09-30)
================================

Improvements to the 'RingPublishingTracking' module.

### Changes

* Events reported while the tracking identifiers are fetched now wait for the identify request
    - on a fresh install the first events (e.g. the first page view) were sent before the identify request answered, without 'eaUUID' in 'ids', so the backend recorded them without 'lu'
    - such events are now sent as soon as the identify request answers, without waiting for the Artemis request; when it fails they are still sent, as before
    - the Artemis identifier in 'RDLU' is still taken when the event is reported, so the very first event of a fresh install can still go out without it
* Identity is requested again after a failed identify request
    - a failed first identify request left the SDK without identifiers for the rest of the session; it is now retried when events are sent, at most once every 30 seconds counted from the end of the previous attempt
    - the identifier fetched by such a retry is delivered with 'didAssignTrackingIdentifier', like the one fetched during 'initialize'
* Events reported after a relaunch, before the Artemis identifier is fetched again, carry the still valid identifier stored by the previous session
    - the stored identifier is kept when the Artemis request gets no answer (e.g. offline) and removed only when the backend rejects the request
* A send requested from a network completion before the post interval passed no longer leaves the events queue with a timer that never fires
